1
00:00:16,328 --> 00:00:17,955
Director Evans.

2
00:00:18,038 --> 00:00:20,833
What? Where did you come from?

3
00:00:20,916 --> 00:00:24,545
I'm sorry, sir. I did knock a few times…

4
00:00:24,628 --> 00:00:27,256
Fine, fine… What do you want?

5
00:00:28,007 --> 00:00:32,011
Um… May I go home for the day?

6
00:00:34,013 --> 00:00:37,349
I'm sorry, sir.
I had plans for this evening…

7
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:41,228
I hadn't realized that managing
your schedule was also my job.

8
00:00:41,312 --> 00:00:44,023
N-No, sir. It's just…

9
00:00:44,106 --> 00:00:47,860
I wanted to celebrate
my son getting into the Academy…

10
00:00:47,943 --> 00:00:52,948
Oh! Well, that's wonderful. We all
look forward to another legacy hire.

11
00:00:53,032 --> 00:00:56,827
Just find someone to fetch the UG2 sample.

12
00:00:56,911 --> 00:01:00,039
Everyone has already
gone home at this hour…

13
00:01:02,083 --> 00:01:05,628
I'll bring over the sample myself… so…

14
00:01:05,711 --> 00:01:10,674
How very kind of you.
Fetch it and get out of my sight.

15
00:01:22,853 --> 00:01:24,522
Director Evans?

16
00:01:33,823 --> 00:01:35,032
Wait…

17
00:01:43,541 --> 00:01:45,417
What happened in there?

18
00:01:46,043 --> 00:01:49,338
Lost you for a sec.
Someone raise a jammer?

19
00:01:49,421 --> 00:01:51,549
Transmission was stable.

20
00:01:52,216 --> 00:01:53,175
Weird.

21
00:01:54,844 --> 00:01:57,972
Yeesh, what a boring gig.

22
00:03:32,024 --> 00:03:36,695
They trespassed on Arasaka premises,
hit us in our own fucking facility.

23
00:03:36,779 --> 00:03:40,950
The lab's research focused
on Militech countermeasures.

24
00:03:41,033 --> 00:03:44,161
Is this related to the runner
who flatlined Jamie and Marcus?

25
00:03:44,245 --> 00:03:46,538
Evans was murdered by a bullet…

26
00:03:46,622 --> 00:03:51,418
This was sloppy, violent.
Safe to say, not the same runner.

27
00:03:51,502 --> 00:03:55,714
Apprehending the netrunner's our priority.
They're too dangerous.

28
00:03:55,798 --> 00:03:58,717
But we know neither
their motive nor purpose…

29
00:03:58,801 --> 00:04:00,886
Whoever they are, they're cautious.

30
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:03,555
Not your average runner looking to score.

31
00:04:03,639 --> 00:04:06,725
We're Arasaka Counterintel.
We never deal with average.

32
00:04:06,809 --> 00:04:10,062
We'll need to take a detour
to catch the runner's trail.

33
00:04:10,145 --> 00:04:13,148
Are we going after Evans' killer?

34
00:04:13,232 --> 00:04:16,986
It's two separate roads.
We may get lucky and find that they merge.

35
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:21,532
Let's switch it up.
We'll go after the fixer.

36
00:04:21,615 --> 00:04:25,327
Who do we know that has ties to Militech?

37
00:04:25,411 --> 00:04:29,415
But if the fixer we get
has ties to the runner,

38
00:04:29,498 --> 00:04:35,004
they could turn around and leak info
about the product to Militech.

39
00:04:35,587 --> 00:04:40,467
They'd be a poor fixer
if they weren't a self-serving bastard.

40
00:04:40,551 --> 00:04:44,805
But at the end of the day,
they're only glorified corporate lapdogs.

41
00:04:45,431 --> 00:04:50,769
We'll just remind them
whose hand they eat off of in this city.

42
00:04:51,353 --> 00:04:53,022
How would you go about this?

43
00:04:54,773 --> 00:04:57,818
We tell them
in the only language this city speaks.

44
00:05:07,536 --> 00:05:08,495
Hey…

45
00:05:15,002 --> 00:05:18,130
Take the fixer! Kill the others!

46
00:05:20,132 --> 00:05:21,258
Grenade!

47
00:05:21,342 --> 00:05:22,343
Go! Go!

48
00:05:41,403 --> 00:05:43,030
I was very nearly killed.

49
00:05:43,113 --> 00:05:45,824
What makes you think it was Arasaka?

50
00:05:45,908 --> 00:05:48,660
Do you take me for a fool?
Who else could it have been?

51
00:05:48,744 --> 00:05:52,039
We're not paying
for any additional liabilities.

52
00:05:52,122 --> 00:05:54,416
And corporate immunity
is still off the table.

53
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:55,667
Are you serious?!

54
00:05:55,751 --> 00:05:59,421
We're already in the red
with your slip-up on the Tanaka case.

55
00:05:59,505 --> 00:06:04,426
With nothing to show for it.
We expect returns on our investments.

56
00:06:04,510 --> 00:06:07,054
Want more resources? Show us results.

57
00:06:07,137 --> 00:06:10,307
And what the hell do you think
I've been chasing?

58
00:06:10,390 --> 00:06:15,687
You're running out of time.
Our patience is running thin.

59
00:06:15,771 --> 00:06:19,191
Arasaka's security
is on higher alert than usual.

60
00:06:19,274 --> 00:06:23,862
Goes to show just how important
the cyberskeleton is to them.

61
00:06:23,946 --> 00:06:25,197
You expect too much.

62
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:30,369
Don't lecture me on the stakes
with all the money we've invested in this.

63
00:06:30,452 --> 00:06:34,373
Not another enny until you earn it.
We're done here.

64
00:06:39,461 --> 00:06:41,505
Damn corporate brat…

65
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:54,351
The fixer's made contact.

66
00:06:55,144 --> 00:06:56,478
As I predicted.

67
00:06:57,062 --> 00:06:59,106
What a good little dog.

68
00:07:07,406 --> 00:07:08,740
David?

69
00:07:11,201 --> 00:07:13,620
Oh, my bad.

70
00:07:13,704 --> 00:07:15,330
Did I wake you up?

71
00:07:15,414 --> 00:07:16,832
Can't sleep?

72
00:07:16,915 --> 00:07:18,584
Couldn't shut my brain off.

73
00:07:19,209 --> 00:07:20,210
Oh.

74
00:07:20,294 --> 00:07:21,128
I'll turn it off.

75
00:07:21,211 --> 00:07:22,754
Aren't you watching?

76
00:07:22,838 --> 00:07:24,840
No, I just had it on…

77
00:07:24,923 --> 00:07:25,757
Oh.

78
00:07:26,425 --> 00:07:31,388
250K to the Moon…
Huh, cheaper than I thought.

79
00:07:31,472 --> 00:07:33,390
For a one-way ticket.

80
00:07:33,474 --> 00:07:35,517
Well, yeah.

81
00:07:36,727 --> 00:07:37,895
You remembered…

82
00:07:37,978 --> 00:07:39,021
Huh?

83
00:07:39,104 --> 00:07:41,231
Nothing. I'm going back to bed.

84
00:07:41,982 --> 00:07:43,650
Okay. 'Night.

85
00:07:51,825 --> 00:07:56,038
The world's greatest corporation
conducting illicit business at a diner.

86
00:07:56,622 --> 00:07:59,791
I thought you'd find
the familiarity reassuring.

87
00:07:59,875 --> 00:08:02,294
I won't pick hairs.
I'm here for your answer.

88
00:08:02,377 --> 00:08:07,424
The cyberskeleton project is
a delicate topic even within Arasaka.

89
00:08:07,508 --> 00:08:11,803
It turned problematic when Tanaka
over-consolidated the operational data.

90
00:08:11,887 --> 00:08:14,431
How much does Militech already know?

91
00:08:14,515 --> 00:08:16,350
Information is the blood of my trade.

92
00:08:16,433 --> 00:08:18,936
I'll need some assurances
before I say any more.

93
00:08:19,019 --> 00:08:23,357
We respect that
you're the best man for the job.

94
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:27,861
We'll gladly provide the compensation
Militech foolishly denied you.

95
00:08:27,945 --> 00:08:30,948
As for the Tanaka mess,
consider your debt settled.

96
00:08:31,031 --> 00:08:32,199
Wonderful.

97
00:08:32,282 --> 00:08:35,577
However, we have some conditions as well.

98
00:08:36,495 --> 00:08:37,454
Let's hear it.

99
00:08:37,538 --> 00:08:42,834
We need to eliminate anyone
who knows about the cyberskeleton.

100
00:08:42,918 --> 00:08:44,503
Done.

101
00:08:44,586 --> 00:08:46,255
And one more thing.

102
00:08:46,338 --> 00:08:47,506
Yes?

103
00:08:47,589 --> 00:08:49,132
After Tanaka died,

104
00:08:49,216 --> 00:08:54,638
there's been a runner interfering
with our recovery on the corrupt data.

105
00:08:54,721 --> 00:08:57,099
Know anything about it?

106
00:08:57,808 --> 00:08:59,059
Not that I can recall.

107
00:08:59,142 --> 00:08:59,977
I see.

108
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:02,938
We're quite curious about this case.

109
00:09:03,021 --> 00:09:08,735
Even if this were Militech,
I can't even imagine why they'd do this.

110
00:09:08,819 --> 00:09:10,654
From what my sources tell me,

111
00:09:10,737 --> 00:09:15,158
no one else knows about Tanaka's ties
to the cyberskeleton project.

112
00:09:15,242 --> 00:09:16,118
An inside job?

113
00:09:16,201 --> 00:09:21,707
No. It's impossible to move internally
without leaving a trail.

114
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:27,379
It's more natural to think that
it's a skilled runner from the outside.

115
00:09:27,462 --> 00:09:30,340
Seems to me like a job for a fixer.

116
00:09:31,008 --> 00:09:32,884
Is this an official commission?

117
00:09:33,468 --> 00:09:38,390
One million to take them alive.
Half the price for their head.

118
00:09:39,850 --> 00:09:41,435
I accept.

119
00:11:20,909 --> 00:11:23,245
Take that!

120
00:11:24,037 --> 00:11:25,205
Out of juice!

121
00:11:25,288 --> 00:11:26,748
Gotcha.

122
00:11:45,892 --> 00:11:47,185
What are you doing?!

123
00:11:48,145 --> 00:11:50,105
Ah… My bad.

124
00:11:51,523 --> 00:11:53,066
Later, David.

125
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:54,151
Yeah…

126
00:11:59,614 --> 00:12:01,199
Falco! Lemme off too!

127
00:12:01,283 --> 00:12:02,325
What?

128
00:12:05,287 --> 00:12:08,039
Well dang,
guess the after-party's just us two.

129
00:12:08,123 --> 00:12:11,042
I've got somewhere to be, too.

130
00:12:11,126 --> 00:12:14,463
That so? Bunch of killjoys,
you, one and all.

131
00:12:15,714 --> 00:12:17,007
David!

132
00:12:19,134 --> 00:12:20,927
No after-party today?

133
00:12:21,011 --> 00:12:23,638
Can't get drunk with those two boomers.

134
00:12:23,722 --> 00:12:26,016
Can't promise I'll be any more fun.

135
00:12:26,099 --> 00:12:27,851
Don't underestimate yourself!

136
00:12:28,643 --> 00:12:30,520
Hey… Wanna take a walk?

137
00:12:30,604 --> 00:12:33,315
Huh? Sure, I guess…

138
00:12:33,398 --> 00:12:34,608
Yes!

139
00:12:38,528 --> 00:12:41,156
So… you doing okay?

140
00:12:41,239 --> 00:12:42,240
What?

141
00:12:42,324 --> 00:12:44,743
What was that today?

142
00:12:44,826 --> 00:12:46,453
What was what?

143
00:12:46,536 --> 00:12:47,787
You know what I mean.

144
00:12:48,413 --> 00:12:49,706
It was nothing.

145
00:12:49,789 --> 00:12:51,833
This isn't the first time it's happened.

146
00:12:52,709 --> 00:12:54,503
You thought I didn't notice?

147
00:12:55,504 --> 00:12:56,630
Whatever.

148
00:12:56,713 --> 00:12:58,757
A girl's intuition, you know?

149
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,841
What girl?

150
00:12:59,925 --> 00:13:01,301
Shut up.

151
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:07,307
You're the only one I watch
that closely, you know.

152
00:13:08,225 --> 00:13:11,520
Come on, David. What's wrong?

153
00:13:12,687 --> 00:13:13,855
Nothing.

154
00:13:13,939 --> 00:13:15,357
I said cut the bull.

155
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,150
It's got nothing to do with you.

156
00:13:17,234 --> 00:13:21,404
Like hell it doesn't.
I'm putting my life in your hands.

157
00:13:22,822 --> 00:13:24,115
Sorry.

158
00:13:26,493 --> 00:13:28,036
I was thinking…

159
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:29,454
Yeah?

160
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,415
You should lay off
the implants for a while.

161
00:13:32,999 --> 00:13:35,168
Don't worry. I've got your back!

162
00:13:35,835 --> 00:13:36,795
You?

163
00:13:36,878 --> 00:13:38,547
I'm being serious.

164
00:13:39,881 --> 00:13:43,218
Remember the psycho
that flatlined my brother?

165
00:13:43,927 --> 00:13:45,262
Yeah.

166
00:13:45,345 --> 00:13:49,432
I don't… wanna see you end up like that.

167
00:13:51,142 --> 00:13:51,977
Yeah.

168
00:14:24,843 --> 00:14:27,846
They're still sending runners?

169
00:14:59,753 --> 00:15:00,629
Hm?

170
00:15:00,712 --> 00:15:03,131
Who are you? W-What the…

171
00:15:34,579 --> 00:15:35,413
Wait…

172
00:16:18,248 --> 00:16:19,624
David!

173
00:16:26,506 --> 00:16:28,591
Rise and shine.

174
00:16:29,217 --> 00:16:30,218
Doc…

175
00:16:30,301 --> 00:16:32,554
Symptoms settling down?

176
00:16:32,637 --> 00:16:33,680
Yeah…

177
00:16:37,809 --> 00:16:39,352
When did it start?

178
00:16:39,436 --> 00:16:40,520
What?

179
00:16:40,603 --> 00:16:44,524
Shaky hands, dizziness,
nausea, usual suspects.

180
00:16:44,607 --> 00:16:47,027
A little while ago.

181
00:16:47,110 --> 00:16:49,320
Why didn't you tell me?

182
00:16:49,404 --> 00:16:51,197
Thought it was temporary.

183
00:16:51,281 --> 00:16:54,325
Looks like side-effects
are finally catching up with you.

184
00:16:54,409 --> 00:16:59,456
Of course, it's crazy enough
how you've been fine until now.

185
00:16:59,539 --> 00:17:01,082
Why now?

186
00:17:01,166 --> 00:17:04,878
Lay off the chrome for a while.

187
00:17:04,961 --> 00:17:08,423
You're already one foot
in the psycho zone.

188
00:17:08,506 --> 00:17:11,092
Then gimme stronger meds for it!

189
00:17:11,176 --> 00:17:16,139
Shit. You ain't hearing me.
Or have you already lost your mind?

190
00:17:16,222 --> 00:17:18,975
Ain't no such miracle drug in exist…

191
00:17:20,393 --> 00:17:26,483
Think I came for jokes?
Take my fucking money…

192
00:17:26,566 --> 00:17:28,902
and gimme the fucking meds!

193
00:17:28,985 --> 00:17:30,361
David!

194
00:17:39,537 --> 00:17:45,126
There. Your last prescription. Nine times
standard dosage, good for nine days.

195
00:17:45,210 --> 00:17:49,756
It'll send you straight over the edge
and right to hell.

196
00:17:50,423 --> 00:17:53,510
I'm sorry. I won't let it happen again.

197
00:17:53,593 --> 00:17:54,719
It's fine.

198
00:17:54,803 --> 00:17:59,891
The fact that you need those meds means
you won't be coming back here anymore.

199
00:18:01,142 --> 00:18:04,896
A kid off the block pushing XBDs and now…

200
00:18:05,688 --> 00:18:10,568
Go be a legend or
whatever the fuck you punks do.

201
00:18:18,618 --> 00:18:20,912
Just another tale for the next dreamer…

202
00:18:21,412 --> 00:18:25,333
David! Wait! What was that?

203
00:18:25,917 --> 00:18:27,335
Don't tell the guys.

204
00:18:28,128 --> 00:18:29,337
I don't understand.

205
00:18:33,424 --> 00:18:34,259
Hey!

206
00:18:39,722 --> 00:18:43,226
Your body, your mind…
They have limits, David. You knew that.

207
00:18:43,309 --> 00:18:46,604
Normal meds don't do it for you anymore.

208
00:18:46,688 --> 00:18:48,064
Isn't it time to call quits?

209
00:18:49,232 --> 00:18:53,987
I can't watch you do this to yourself.
Scale back your cyberware…

210
00:18:54,654 --> 00:18:56,114
I can't do that.

211
00:18:56,197 --> 00:18:57,073
Why not?

212
00:18:58,116 --> 00:19:02,328
Mom and Maine…
They all left me something to do.

213
00:19:03,329 --> 00:19:05,331
But I haven't done nothing yet.

214
00:19:05,415 --> 00:19:08,793
But you can't keep going on like this…

215
00:19:08,877 --> 00:19:11,004
I'll be fine.

216
00:19:11,087 --> 00:19:15,550
How could you say that?
Do you really think you're special?

217
00:19:16,634 --> 00:19:21,139
I withstood the Sandevistan.
I'm not normal.

218
00:19:22,515 --> 00:19:28,354
So you're a little more sturdy than
everyone else. But you're still human.

219
00:19:31,232 --> 00:19:32,859
I shot a woman.

220
00:19:32,942 --> 00:19:33,776
Huh?

221
00:19:35,111 --> 00:19:38,156
She was around the same age as my mom.

222
00:19:38,907 --> 00:19:40,658
She also had a son like me.

223
00:19:42,994 --> 00:19:45,622
A harmless bystander. A normal person.

224
00:19:47,123 --> 00:19:50,126
I don't know how many I've killed anymore.

225
00:19:51,753 --> 00:19:54,130
It doesn't even make me pause anymore.

226
00:19:55,506 --> 00:19:59,010
Maybe I really am going crazy.

227
00:19:59,636 --> 00:20:00,553
David…

228
00:20:01,471 --> 00:20:05,225
I ain't normal.
Like you said before, I'm different.

229
00:20:05,308 --> 00:20:06,643
You're not.

230
00:20:06,726 --> 00:20:08,019
I am!

231
00:20:08,728 --> 00:20:10,355
You're not.

232
00:20:10,438 --> 00:20:12,148
You wouldn't understand.

233
00:20:13,608 --> 00:20:17,028
You left the crew after Maine died.

234
00:20:17,111 --> 00:20:18,529
That's because…

235
00:20:18,613 --> 00:20:20,281
I'm not blaming you.

236
00:20:20,365 --> 00:20:21,532
Why not?

237
00:20:21,616 --> 00:20:24,410
You shouldn't have to live this life.

238
00:20:24,494 --> 00:20:27,914
No, David. That's not what I…

239
00:20:27,997 --> 00:20:30,833
Then you'll come back?

240
00:20:30,917 --> 00:20:34,337
Let's go back to the way things were,
working together.

241
00:20:38,424 --> 00:20:41,678
I can't right now.
Wait for me a little while longer.

242
00:20:41,761 --> 00:20:42,595
What for?

243
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:46,307
There's something I need to do first.

244
00:20:46,391 --> 00:20:48,142
Like what?

245
00:20:48,226 --> 00:20:49,811
I can't say.

246
00:20:50,436 --> 00:20:51,521
Why?

247
00:20:51,604 --> 00:20:52,563
Sorry.

248
00:20:53,231 --> 00:20:55,024
Because you don't trust me.

249
00:20:55,733 --> 00:20:57,026
I'm sorry.

250
00:20:58,111 --> 00:21:01,197
Okay. I'll stop asking you about it.

251
00:21:01,281 --> 00:21:02,115
Okay.

252
00:21:03,741 --> 00:21:07,453
Maybe we should go our separate ways.

253
00:21:08,204 --> 00:21:10,623
No! That's not true David.

254
00:21:18,131 --> 00:21:21,884
I'm sorry, David. I have to go.

255
00:21:21,968 --> 00:21:24,387
Huh? Where?

256
00:21:25,847 --> 00:21:27,223
I have to go…

257
00:21:29,309 --> 00:21:30,768
Okay.

258
00:21:30,852 --> 00:21:32,395
We'll talk when I get home.

259
00:21:33,104 --> 00:21:34,939
Wait for me.

260
00:21:49,203 --> 00:21:51,789
The same ID as the runner from before.

261
00:21:52,957 --> 00:21:54,334
There you are…

262
00:22:19,150 --> 00:22:22,362
Didn't think it would be so easy.

263
00:22:26,324 --> 00:22:29,952
This is our passport into Arasaka.

264
00:22:30,036 --> 00:22:32,330
Excellent job, Kiwi.
